The OSF book "Introduction to OSF(TM) DCE" also has a short but complete
example, with all code, in Section 3.8.  It is for a "very simple
distributed application called greet." It "...is implemented two ways
-- one using DCE RPC, the other using DCE DFS.  "The client... sends a
greeting to the server....  The Server prints the client's greeting
and sends a greeting back to the client.  The client prints the
server's reply and terminates."  The two implementations, including
instructions, take up less than 13 pages.

The Introduction to OSF DCE is published by Prentice Hall, ISBN
0-13-490624.
 
