No, it is not. See Kernighan & Pike, "The Unix Programming
Environment", p.18.  grep was constructed in an evening by Ken
Thompson, by yanking the code out of ed (which he had also written)
and creating a stand-alone program out of it. The ed command was

	g/re/p

which stands for "Globally look for Regular Expression and Print". 
Whether you want to say that it is an acronym or a literal reading
of the ed command is up to you.


